# Development

## Set up

```bash
npm install                     # also installs the git hooks (lefthook)
npx playwright install chromium # once per machine, for the screenshot check
```

The workflow security hook runs zizmor through `uvx`, so it needs
[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/).

## Quality gates

Every gate is a hook in `lefthook.yml`. CI runs the same hooks with
`--all-files`, so passing locally means passing in CI.

| Gate | Tool | Runs on |
|---|---|---|
| Lint and format | Biome | commit |
| Types, strict | TypeScript | commit |
| Colours come from theme tokens, not hex values or palette classes | `scripts/check-colours.mjs` | commit |
| Workflow security | zizmor | commit, when workflows change |
| Every button does something, or is a `NotBuiltButton` that says it is not built | `scripts/check-inert-buttons.mjs` | commit |
| Text sizes on the type scale (11 to 18, then 20, 22, 28, 32, 40, 48, 56, 72 px) | `scripts/check-type-scale.mjs` | commit |
| No AI co-author trailers | `scripts/check-no-ai-coauthors.mjs` | commit message |
| Build | Vite | push |
| Screenshots in light and dark, desktop, laptop and phone; no broken chart, console error, spilling panel, sideways scroll or colliding chart label | `scripts/check.mjs` and `scripts/layout-checks.mjs` | push |
[%- if artifact %]
| Artifact page: light/dark switching, charts and phone layout inside an artifact-like host | `scripts/check-artifact.mjs` | push |
[%- endif %]

```bash
npx lefthook run pre-commit --all-files
npx lefthook run pre-push --all-files
```

CI also audits runtime dependencies with `npm audit`, weekly as well as on
every change, and keeps the screenshots as a downloadable run artifact.

## Theme

`theme` in `app.config.json` picks the direction: `instrument`, `editorial` or
`console`. `THEME=<name> npm run dev` tries another one without changing the
file. Light or dark follows the system setting; `data-theme="light"` or
`"dark"` on `<html>` overrides it.

The theme package lives in `theme/` and comes from atelier; don't edit it
here.
[%- if artifact %]

## Artifact

`npm run build:artifact` writes `dist/artifact/index.html`: page content only,
fonts from Google Fonts, everything else inlined, as claude.ai artifacts
require. `npm run check:artifact` loads it in an artifact-like host first.
[%- endif %]
[%- if pages %]

## GitHub Pages

On push to `main`, the pages workflow publishes the app. Enable Pages once
under Settings › Pages with "GitHub Actions" as the source.
[%- endif %]

## Dependencies

Dependabot proposes grouped weekly updates for npm and GitHub Actions,
skipping versions younger than a week. Actions are pinned by commit hash.

## Template updates

Pull later atelier improvements, including theme and component fixes, with:

```bash
uvx copier update --trust
```
